13 minute workouts 20 minute recipes 10  minute mindfulness ready to become get  feel on the App Store or Google Play I  grew up eating Indian food often and I  love the rich flavors that go into the  dishes sadly with a lot of takeaways  Indian food often get a bad rap for  being high in calories and extremely  unhealthy well this is not entirely true  when you cook at home you can control  what goes into the dish and you can make  them extremely healthy so I'm going to  share with you an Indian inspired meal  prep which is easy to follow delicious  and nutritious for lunch we're going to  make chicken and fish tandoori skewers  served with cucumber salad as for dinner  we're making a part of light vegetable  curry to be served with rice let's start  with lunch tandoori is such a popular  Indian dish and it is healthy what's  there not to love about it the meats are  often cooked in a clay oven but for this  we're going to use a regular oven I'm  going to use a 400 grams of chicken  breast and 400 grams of white fish you  can choose any other meats of your  choice as for vegan you can substitute  the meat for tofu or vegetables for the  marinade you'll need one and a half  tablespoons of olive oil have a cup of  plain yogurt four garlic cloves roughly  chopped 2 tablespoons of fresh ginger  roughly chopped 1 teaspoon of ground  coriander cumin and turmeric and 1/2 a  teaspoon of white pepper as well as one  tablespoon of paprika and salt to taste  now let's start cooking cube the chicken  breasts into chunks and slice the fish  in a blender add the garlic and ginger  along with a splash of water and blend  to make a thick smooth paste now in a  separate bowl add the blended garlic and  ginger paste along with the rest of the  marinade ingredients oil lemon juice  yogurt and all the spices mix well  marinate the chicken breast cubes and  fish slices  and live them for 15 to 20 minutes for  the meat to soak all the flavors in now  let's preheat the oven to 220 degrees  Celsius after 50 minutes skewer the  chicken with wooden skewers and place  them on a baking tray if you don't have  the wooden skewers you can just place  the chicken of fish fillets onto the  baking tray that is absolutely fine as  well  now we want to bake them in the oven for  15 to 20 minutes until the meats are  golden so I'm serving this dish with  cucumber salad or as it is called  Kitumba salad this is a fresh crunchy  salad that doesn't need any cooking and  can be put together very quickly it is a  perfect side dish what you'll need are  half a cup of chopped onions 1 cup of  chopped tomatoes 1 cup of chopped  cucumber cut a cup of chopped fresh  coriander 1 teaspoon of red chili powder  2 tablespoons of freshly squeezed lemon  juice and salt to taste chopped up all  the vegetables and simply add all the  ingredients into a bowl mix well we want  to chill the salad in the fridge until  it is ready to be served lunch is ready  I love the light laminate taste and  slightly spicy flavors of the chicken  and fish tandoori served with the  refreshing cucumber salad this dish is  high in protein and gluten free each  serving of chicken and fish tandoori  with cucumber salad has about 380  calories and 55 grams of protein now  because the meats are could dry they  make a great meal prep dish which you  can bring it out with you and will last  for a long time if you want to you can  also serve this with roti or basmati  rice as for dinner we're making  chickpeas and vegetable curry served  with a purse Mathew rice curries can be  complicated and time-consuming we're  going to keep it really simple and quick  this easy vegan one pot dish is packed  with flavors from a combination of  spices with its smooth  creamy texture what you'll need are 300  grams of Carens cut into cubes 200 grams  of spinach fresh or frozen 1 can of  chickpeas rinsed and drained 1 can of  diced tomatoes 1/2 a cup of light  coconut milk 1 tbsp of olive oil 1  medium onion diced 6 garlic cloves  minced a thumb sized piece of ginger  minced 1 tbsp of cumin 1 tablespoon of  curry powder 1 teaspoon of paprika and  salt and pepper to taste  saute the onion and garlic with olive  oil until tender and golden brown just  for 2 to 3 minutes then add in the  ginger and all the spices and salt and  pepper mix all the spices together  before adding in the diced tomatoes  spinach chick peas and carrots then stir  in the coconut milk reduce the heat to  low and cook everything together for 10  to 15 minutes before serving don't  forget to stir occasionally so I'm gonna  serve this with a side of my favorite  long grain basmati rice you may also  choose to serve it with roti quinoa or  jasmine rice so what I love about this  recipe is that you can keep it versatile  by simply changing up the vegetables  bins or even add meat into the curry you  can even double the recipe and cook it  for a large family so each serving with  1 cup of basmati rice has about 476  calories all these recipes were keep  well in the fridge for up to 3 days if  you're planning to prep your meal for  the entire week then store them in the  freezer as simply warm them up when you  want to have your meals so when you're  in the mood for Indian food instead of  ordering a takeaway make these recipes  in your kitchen don't forget to give  this video a thumbs up share this video  on with your friends and do remember to  subscribe to my youtube channel for a  lot more healthy recipes workout videos  as well as nutritional tips let me know  in the comments below what are the milk  prep or recipes do you want more off all  the best
 

